            <ArticleTitle>Patellofemoral pain syndrome in Tibetan Buddhist monks.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>129-31</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Patellofemoral pain syndrome is a common diagnosis in athletes and especially runners. This article discusses 3 cases of patellofemoral pain caused by pronounced inactivity and prolonged knee hyperflexion at altitude in a unique population of Tibetan Buddhist monks. In this case, the monks responded well to a program of activity modification and exercises.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
